hash-table or hash-map use arrays under the hood.
in arrays search base on index is O(1),
hash-table or hash-map have some technic on arrays!
they want to make search base on some value (the key) as O(1)

if we can map the key to some numeric value,  (hash value)
and then map this numeric value to a index ,  (index value)
we can find that key by index!


HASH FUNCTION
hash function is a function that gets a value and maps it to a different kind of value,
we call this new value as "hash-code" or "hash-value" or "digest"
in context of data structure, a hash function maps a key value to an index value.
(hash-value is not always used for DS)

there are so many algorithm to calculate hashes,
some of them used in CRYPTOGRAPHY, like hashing password on DB.
so in the context of cryptography this hash value is not index value!
but in the context of DS, we use hash value to create index value!



JAVA HASH FUNCTION
in JAVA, every obj has a method called hashCode().
it is Object class method.
this method convert the obj to a hash value.
it is not on the context of DS, so it is not index value!
it just a hash value.

the HashMap class that we have in JAVA, use this hash code
and then it does some extra work to map it to an index value


Note: specific classes like String, Integer, ...
      have override hashCode()
      they create hash code based on their values.
      but in general (the hashCode() on Object class)
      the hash code created based on the addresses of obj.
      so each obj will have different hash.


